Description: rkmpp decoders: drop the static output pix_fmts advertisement
 The ffmpeg-rockchip *_rkmpp decoders declared a static AVCodec.pix_fmts
 array (NV12/NV16/NV15/NV20/NV24/DRM_PRIME). That field is metadata only:
 the decoders negotiate their real output format at runtime by building a
 local {DRM_PRIME, <sw_fmt>} list and calling ff_get_format(), and nothing
 reads the static array. Upstream FFmpeg's own rkmpp decoder does not set it,
 and the libavcodec-avcodec self-test (libavcodec/tests/avcodec.c) rejects any
 video decoder that sets pix_fmts or supported_framerates, which aborts
 `make check`.
 .
 Remove the static array and its CODEC_PIXFMTS_ARRAY() reference so the
 decoders match upstream and pass the self-test. The DRM_PRIME hw_config that
 players (Kodi's DRM PRIME codec, mpv) rely on is unchanged, and runtime
 format negotiation is unaffected.
Author: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-07-11
--- a/libavcodec/rkmppdec.h
+++ b/libavcodec/rkmppdec.h
@@ -104,16 +104,6 @@ static const AVOption options[] = {
     { NULL }
 };
 
-static const enum AVPixelFormat rkmpp_dec_pix_fmts[] = {
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NV12,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NV16,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NV15,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NV20_PACKED,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NV24,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME,
-    AV_PIX_FMT_NONE,
-};
-
 static const AVCodecHWConfigInternal *const rkmpp_dec_hw_configs[] = {
     &(const AVCodecHWConfigInternal) {
         .public = {
@@ -151,7 +141,6 @@ const FFCodec ff_##x##_rkmpp_decoder = { \
     .caps_internal  = FF_CODEC_CAP_NOT_INIT_THREADSAFE | \
                       FF_CODEC_CAP_INIT_CLEANUP | \
                       FF_CODEC_CAP_SETS_FRAME_PROPS, \
-    CODEC_PIXFMTS_ARRAY(rkmpp_dec_pix_fmts), \
     .hw_configs     = rkmpp_dec_hw_configs, \
     .p.wrapper_name = "rkmpp", \
 };
